Prop item loads have been added, so they should start appearing
in The World more over time. Currently only three zones feature them:
Gnomish Wonders, Tsirin Prison, and Upper Cimea. And yes, that means
everyone's favorite backstabber is anxiously awaiting his first victims.

Prop items are exactly the same as the normal version of an item,
except they can't be rented or sold and decay after about 8 real-life
hours.

Props will appear on mobs **when they spawn**, which is intentional.
Load-on-death is still active otherwise, so if you see a mob wielding
an item or wearing armor it's almost definitely a prop.

The usage of prop items is up to builders, as they're added via
zonefiles. Their primary purpose is to make fights more difficult,
interesting, and dynamic.

Mobs equipped with prop weapons and armor might do more damage, take
less damage, be protected from certain insta-kill crits, cause players
to damage their weapons when striking the mobs' prop armor, and be able
to use skills players aren't expecting a mob to use (for example, backstab
or stab), etc.

The secondary purpose of prop items is to act as a temporary reward for
winning a fight, if the mob fails to load the real thing on death.

If you notice anything weird, broken, or overpowered please let an imm
know in game or mention it on Discord.
